{
  "about": "The characters a tool-approval surface shows as <U+XXXX> instead of themselves: Unicode 16.0's Cc, Cf, Default_Ignorable_Code_Point, unassigned code points (Cn, the noncharacters included: they have no agreed appearance, and macOS draws some as an empty cell with an advance) and private-use code points (Co: they look like whatever a font puts there, and Apple's system fonts draw some as nothing, with no width), every White_Space character but the plain space U+0020 (U+2028, U+2029, the no-break, Ogham, en to hair, narrow no-break, math and ideographic spaces), U+2800 BRAILLE PATTERN BLANK and U+FFFC OBJECT REPLACEMENT CHARACTER (which Apple's text engine draws as an empty cell a space wide), less \\n and \\t, which the pretty-printed arguments' own layout uses. Inclusive ranges of hex code points, sorted and disjoint. A one-line field (a tool name, an agent id) has no layout of its own, so it also shows line_adds escaped: \\t and \\n, as ranges of the same shape, outside ranges. Its set is ranges plus line_adds, and line_cases are worked cases of it. One table for two languages: the Rust side (openalpaca_core::utils::text::needs_escape, escape_hidden, hidden_notice, needs_escape_in_line, escape_hidden_line) is held equal to every range, case and notice here by a test that reads this file; the GUI derives its set from it. suggestion_cases are worked counts of one memory suggestion's five fields (openalpaca_core::memory::service::suggestion_hidden: the titles and the reason with the one-line set, the excerpt and the knowledge with ranges), and cut_notices the words a cut text ends with (cut_notice). Change both sides together.",
